WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:04.200
When I first finished Dark Souls 3, I barely found any NPC's

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.880
and I think that's going to be a really common thing for most people.

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:11.320
It's easy, in this game, to miss a part of their questline,

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:12.820
and then leave them behind.

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:17.080
So this video is going to help you at least start their questlines,

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:19.840
so you have a higher chance of running into them later.

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:23.240
First up is Ringfinder Leonhard.

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:27.180
You find him early on in the game, standing by Lothric's throne.

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:30.200
Talk to him, and he'll give you five cracked Red Eye Orbs

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:35.100
which you can use to invade other players, to get a Pale Tongue reward.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.880
You need this Pale Tongue to continue his questline.

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:41.180
An easy way to get a Pale Tongue is to shoot this hanging corpse

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:44.220
after the Siegward encounter in the Undead Settlement

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:44.720
(ah)

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:46.360
which we'll get to in a little bit.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:49.500
So once you have the Tongue, talk to Leonhard back at the throne

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:55.900
and he'll give you a key to the Darkwraiths' cell below the second bonfire on the High Wall of Lothric.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:01:00.420
Kill the Darkwraith for the Red Eye Orb, so you can invade an infinite amount of times

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:04.540
and then you'll find Leonhard back at Firelink, where he commends you.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:09.980
Then, when you reach the Cathedral of The Deep, you'll have the option to join Rosaria's Covenant.

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:14.140
Join, and then offer a Pale Tongue, and you'll see Leonhard behind you.

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:20.080
Talk to him and then check back at Rosaria later in the game to continue his questline.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:21.660
Be warned though,

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:28.040
Joining Rosaria's Covenant makes an NPC named Sirris hostile for the rest of your playthrough.

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:32.560
Sirris is of the Darkmoon line, which is in opposition to Rosaria's Covenant

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:39.220
and her questline, if you do it, leads to her armor, her shield, her talisman and a few other items.

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:41.040
If you don't talk to Rosaria, though

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:44.460
Sirris's summon sign will appear throughout your late game

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:48.480
and you can enter her world and assist her in certain places.

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:52.880
Also, back in Firelink Shrine, is Ludleth of Courland

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:55.760
who you've might have missed, because he's so tiny :)

00:01:55.760 --> 00:02:00.360
but once you've killed the Rotten Greatwood you can give him the Transposing Kiln

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:03.640
in order to make boss weapons out of boss souls.

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:06.520
Another questline to initiate is Greirat's.

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:10.000
Warp to the second bonfire upon Lothric's High Wall

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:14.680
and then head directly down as soon as you encounter the black mass.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:18.980
Find his cell key in the cellar area at the botton of these stairs

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:23.280
and then unlock his cell at the area below the second bonfire.

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:28.680
He appears back in your shrine after this and asks you to bring him Loretta's bone

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:32.960
which is found on the balcony of the first building in the Undead Settlement.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:36.380
After this, you keep talking to him back here in the shrine and

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:39.000
he will eventually offer to go pillaging.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:43.640
He will return once you kill a boss and he'll come back with some new loot.

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:48.760
As you continue through the game, he'll offer to go pillaging again in the future, but...

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:52.720
it is increasingly difficult to keep him alive later on so,

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:55.340
we'll get to his questline in episode two.

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:59.720
Also, in the Undead Settlment is Yoel, at the end of the first bridge.

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:04.720
He comes back to your shrine and teaches you sorceries there, but that's not the main thing he does.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:07.980
He also gives you free levels at the cost of hollowing.

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:11.740
Now, I explained the hollowing mechanic in my gameplay secrets video

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:16.660
but basically, if you want to progress his questline - choose to "Draw out your true strength"

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:20.580
and then throw yourself to your death in Firelink Shrine over and over

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:24.620
coming back to Yoel often, to just level up every few times you die.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:31.420
After five levels, Yuria appears, whose story eventually intertwines with Anri and Horaces'.

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:34.160
Anri is found after the Road of Sacrifices.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:40.700
His or her, depending on your gender, their questline continues after you kill the Deacons of The Deep.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:44.360
So make sure you talk to her after the Road of Sacrifices

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:47.840
and then back in your shrine after the Deacons of The Deep.

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:48.400
Now,

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:50.880
Anri's questline gets god damned tricky:

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:53.940
there are many branching paths, there are many ways to fail

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:56.140
and there are multiple ways to complete it

00:03:56.140 --> 00:04:00.380
and because of these reasons and others, it's actually my favourite questline.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:04.140
So. we're going to talk about it in the Lore-through-series if you're interested.

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:07.680
We're gonna examine it from every angle and go through every bit of the story line

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.260
because it is fantastic &lt;3

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:15.900
Another fantastic story is Siegward's, which you initiate at the elevator in the Undead Settlement

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:18.900
and this is a questline you'll want to start and complete for sure

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:22.760
To start it, send the elevator down alone, ride it back up again

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:26.900
befriend the giant atop the tower and then jump off the elevator

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:29.820
halfway down when you hear... "Hmm".

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:34.820
Kill the Fire Demon with Siegward and have a toast with your new best friend :)

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:39.280
Now, the tough part of Siegward's questline is something I think a ton of you  guys would have missed

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:40.980
and if you found it - great job!

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:42.200
It's really out of the way.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:47.140
So, outside of the Cleansing Chapel bonfire near the Cathedral of The Deep

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:49.560
is Siegward stuck down a well :(

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:55.680
I think he spawns here after the Abyss Watchers, but you might just want to check back here regularely.

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:58.920
Siegwards is down there and he's lost his armour

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:00.920
Someone stole it - guess who...

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:40.840
I had a huge amount of trouble, getting Patches to spawn here but I finally figured it out.

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:44.760
I made sure that I opened the huge door  in the swampy area

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:47.960
and then the huge door right before this bridge

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:52.780
then I reloaded the game, taking note of the fact that the bridge was still down.

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:57.580
When I reloaded, Patches had entered and raised the bridge for me.

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:00.800
The thing is, this part of the quest is entirely optional

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:03.360
so as soon as you find Siegward down the well

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:07.020
go back to Firelink, buy the Tower Key from the handmaiden

00:06:07.020 --> 00:06:10.220
and then head up the elevator behind the shrine.

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:13.760
You'll hear and see the door below close behind you

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:17.540
and when you get back down, you'll see a familiar face on the other side.

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:20.700
To get back to him, jump down off the side here.

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:27.480
Or, you can warp back to Firelink and then confront Patches on the upper right path.

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:30.940
You can buy Siegward's armor from him or kill him for it.

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:34.980
Bring this armor to Siegward in the well, drop it down for him and

00:06:34.980 --> 00:06:38.680
both questlines, Patches and Siegward, continue from here.

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:42.900
Look out for Siegward when you get into a kitchen in Irithyll.

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:45.920
The next four questlines relate to the class you're playing as

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:49.920
so if you're playing as a Pyromancer, a Cleric or a Sorcerer.

00:06:50.360 --> 00:06:54.940
If you want pyromancy, find Cornyx in his cage in the Undead Settlement.

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:58.780
Turn right at the burning tree, go through the building after the bridge

00:06:58.780 --> 00:07:02.540
and then look for this drop-down near the fire bomb throwing enemies.

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:06.140
Hit the bonfire, head up and free Cornyx from his cage.

00:07:06.340 --> 00:07:10.080
Cornyx appears here in your shrine, and he'll give you a Pyromancy Hand

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:13.540
and give you pyromancy spells if you give him the tomes.

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:17.940
If you want access to miracles and dark magic, then you have to free Irina.

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:22.900
Get the Mortician's Ashes from the arrow graveyard past the Delapidated Bridge bonfire

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:29.680
bring it to the Handmaiden, buy the Grave Key, unlock the door in the sewers and free Irina in her cell.

00:07:29.940 --> 00:07:36.040
She'll appear here in your shrine and will teach you miracles if you bring her the Braille Tomes for it.

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:40.760
And  if you want to learn sorcery, we mentioned that Yoel sells sorceries, but really...

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:44.740
the best spells are sold by Orbeck in the Crucifiction Woods.

00:07:45.140 --> 00:07:51.800
You get to Orbeck by entering this ruined keep, and then turning left at this bridge with the spear hollow.

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:53.700
If you're not &gt;stupid and you have ten intellect,

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:58.900
then Orbeck will agree to come back to your shrine and teach you in return for scrolls

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:04.880
and be aware - you need to actually bring him scrolls or he might disappear from your shrine, I've heard.

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:11.820
And if you want to learn dark miracles or dark pyromancies, then you have to rescue an NPC named Karla.

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:17.820
Karla can be rescued in a cell in Irithyll Dungeon once you find the Jailor's Cell Key.

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:22.300
Her cell is located in the rectangular room  with the swarm of jailors

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:27.320
and the key itself is located far further below, in the Profaned Capital.

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:32.060
Go past the toxic swamp, go up the rooftop and through this doorway.

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:40.140
She teaches dark miracles back at Firelink, below Andre, and she can also accept two dark pyromancy tomes.

00:08:40.380 --> 00:08:44.460
Hawkwood will eventually disappear from Firelink, you might have noticed

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:46.760
and he's found his purpose.

00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:51.360
You'll encounter him again once you make your way through the hidden Dragon Shrine

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:57.680
which you find by performing the Way of Dragon-emote at the cliff face in Irithyll Dungeon.

00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:00.240
You get the emote after Oceiros.

00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:04.340
After you clear this area, talk to Andre and he'll give you a note

00:09:04.340 --> 00:09:08.180
that Hawkwood left for you to progress the questline.

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:14.540
The Firekeeper has no real quest per se, but she does have a few items that she reacts to

00:09:14.660 --> 00:09:19.400
which extend her dialogue options and her significance as an NPC.

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:24.320
First is the Firekeeper Soul, atop Firelink Shrine that you reach with the Tower Key

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:27.100
and the second is very much in the late game.

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:35.240
These are the Eyes of a Firekeeper and they're found behind an illusory wall in the Darkened Firelink Shrine.

00:09:35.820 --> 00:09:41.200
So later on, I'll make a video on how to finish all of these questlines in multiple different ways

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:45.640
because there's so many branching paths and ways to fail them, as I mentioned.

00:09:45.840 --> 00:09:48.180
But (uh) do your playthrough with just these tips in mind

00:09:48.180 --> 00:09:52.760
and see how many you can complete naturally first. I think that's a fun way to do it.

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:56.620
(ah) come back to the channel to figure out how to do them every way.

00:09:56.780 --> 00:10:01.820
You can also check out these two videos where we go over some of the more obscure secrets of the early game.

00:10:01.840 --> 00:10:03.420
There's some neat stuff in there.

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:06.860
And I wanna shout out another video I helped do the gameplay for

00:10:07.020 --> 00:10:10.120
It's by a Youtube channel named Wisecrack

00:10:10.340 --> 00:10:13.780
and they do a ton of really interesting (uh) philosophical takes on media

00:10:13.780 --> 00:10:19.120
and they have a... very unique take on the Dark Souls franchise, if you're interested.

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:22.660
They're always well produced videos even if you don't agree with what they say

00:10:22.660 --> 00:10:25.080
so thanks for watching guys. I'll see you in the next one

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:30.280
and next week we are going really hard at the lore. So look forward to that.

00:10:30.280 --> 00:10:30.840
Bye bye.

